WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.840
The Game of Thrones guys are getting out of
the galaxy far, far away.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:10.060
David Benioff and D.B. Weiss, best known for
creating and showrunning Game of Thrones,

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:13.600
have exited Lucasfilm and their planned Star
Wars trilogy.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:18.279
The pair were slated to write and direct three
films that would have served as the next chapter

00:00:18.279 --> 00:00:23.730
in the Star Wars franchise following the launch
of The Rise of Skywalker, the final installment

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:26.000
in the nine-film Skywalker saga.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.920
Benioff and Weiss revealed in a statement
why they are no longer making their Star Wars

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:34.920
trilogy: they are simply too busy working
on projects for Netflix.

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:40.560
In August 2019, it was reported that the duo
had inked a massive five-year deal, believed

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:45.020
to be worth as much as $300 million, with
the streaming giant to create new television

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:46.620
series and original movies.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:51.280
No details on Benioff and Weiss' Netflix shows
and films have been revealed as of the making

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:55.540
of this video, but it seems clear that they
may be more invested in those projects than

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:57.320
in their three Star Wars films.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:02.820
Still, the joint statement that Benioff and
Weiss provided to Deadline alongside the announcement

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:07.700
indicates that their decision to depart from
the Star Wars universe had no ill intent,

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:12.090
and that the move wasn't motivated by any
bad blood or behind-the-scenes troubles.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.220
It read, in part,

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:15.080
"We love Star Wars.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:17.920
When George Lucas built it, he built us too.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:22.100
Getting to talk about Star Wars with him and
the current Star Wars team was the thrill

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:26.079
of a lifetime, and we will always be indebted
to the saga that changed everything.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:31.340
There are only so many hours in the day, and
we felt we could not do justice to both Star

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Wars and our Netflix projects.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.420
So we are regretfully stepping away."

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:40.100
Lucasfilm president Kathleen Kennedy echoed
Benioff and Weiss' sentiments in a statement

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.120
of her own, writing,

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:44.860
"David Benioff and Dan Weiss are incredible
storytellers.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.659
We hope to include them in the journey forward
when they are able to step away from their

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:50.760
busy schedule to focus on Star Wars."

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:55.740
Judging by the remarks Benioff, Weiss, and
Kennedy made, it appears that everything is

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:58.580
pretty peachy-keen between the creatives and
the studio.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:03.860
However, some Thrones fans have begun theorizing
that perhaps this isn't the entire truth,

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:08.959
and that Lucasfilm may have actually fired
Benioff and Weiss over their polarizing handling

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:10.840
of the final season of Game of Thrones.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:13.280
"My heart is broken!"

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:14.800
"Don't touch me."

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:18.480
This, of course, is all just speculation.

00:02:18.489 --> 00:02:23.129
The upside of all of this is that the Star
Wars franchise will be just fine without Benioff

00:02:23.129 --> 00:02:24.100
and Weiss on board.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:29.380
Lucasfilm is far smarter than to have the
future success of the entire film series hinge

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:31.510
on the enduring commitment of two people.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:36.400
Plus, the studio has plenty of time to get
its proverbial TIE Fighters in a row and decide

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:40.409
who should take the reins on the franchise
moving forward, as the Star Wars films will

00:02:40.409 --> 00:02:44.800
be taking a brief hiatus following the December
20th premiere of The Rise of Skywalker.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:50.040
It's believed that the break will last three
years, given that the first of Benioff and

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:55.800
Weiss' three Star Wars installments was expected
to hit cinemas sometime in 2022.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:00.820
One might assume that Lucasfilm would have
to delay the franchise return by a year or

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:04.860
two to make up for the loss of Benioff and
Weiss and the creative shake-ups that will

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:09.780
ensue, but don't forget that the studio has
two big-name movie-makers already working

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:14.489
on projects of their own, creatives who are
more than capable of taking the place of Benioff

00:03:14.489 --> 00:03:15.140
and Weiss.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:20.920
Both The Last Jedi writer-director Rian Johnson
and Marvel Studios chief creative officer

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:26.390
Kevin Feige are set to create their own additions
to the Star Wars universe, with Johnson making

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:29.760
his own trilogy and Feige on board to produce
one movie.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:34.840
It seems most plausible that Lucasfilm will
effectively replace Benioff and Weiss' trilogy

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:39.360
with Johnson's, though there's no way to know
what the studio will do at this point in time.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:43.020
Either way, the future of Star Wars still
looks bright.

